& [CollisionFinding] distinguishes ownership from integration
  + I03A alone owns workspace Cargo dependency feature and lock mutation
  + I03B I03C and I03D each propose modifying lib.rs while owning different modules
  + I03E I03E1 I03E2 and I03E3 all require implementation under the same report concern and could collapse into one oversized file
  + shared-file touch is not itself a defect when changes are serialized and prerequisite-bound
  + parallel unleased edits to lib.rs conformance/mod.rs Cargo.toml Cargo.lock or fixture catalogues are forbidden

& [ModuleTopology] assigns one semantic owner per implementation module
  + I03B owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/json_ingress.rs
  + I03C owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/residual_registry.rs
  + I03D owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/reader_observation.rs and production CantorDenyRetriever
  + I03E1 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/obligation.rs
  + I03E2 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/proposal.rs
  + I03E3 owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/review.rs
  + I03E owns crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/report.rs
  + crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/conformance/mod.rs is a declaration and re-export ledger only
  + crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/lib.rs is a crate integration and re-export ledger only
  + semantic implementation in either integration ledger is forbidden

& [TestTopology] mirrors ownership
  + I03A owns tests/schema_validator_dependency.rs
  + I03B owns tests/json_ingress.rs
  + I03C owns tests/residual_registry.rs
  + I03D owns tests/reader_observation.rs
  + I03E1 owns tests/conformance_obligation.rs
  + I03E2 owns tests/conformance_proposal.rs
  + I03E3 owns tests/conformance_review.rs
  + I03E owns tests/conformance_report.rs
  + common fixtures may be referenced by several tests but each fixture has one generating authority and immutable content identity

& [CompileTimeCorpusTopology] separates inventories from implementation
  + tests/fixtures/cpms_i03/ is the candidate root for immutable source and expectation bytes
  + exact subpaths are assigned only by a future signed activation inventory
  + every admitted fixture path role bytes SHA256 generator identity predecessor and owning slice are enumerated
  + catalogue order is canonical and content addressed
  + no runtime scan directory discovery file write cache database or mutable fixture update is permitted
  + source schemas and current goldens remain immutable inputs rather than copied ownership

& [IntegrationLedgerRule] serializes shared surfaces
  + one activated unit at a time receives an exact TouchLease for a shared file
  + the lease binds predecessor digest expected semantic delta allowed line-independent anchors and successor digest
  + lib.rs changes may only declare cfg-gated modules and public re-exports already authorized by the unit
  + conformance/mod.rs changes may only declare and re-export one newly authorized conformance child
  + Cargo files may change only in I03A and only under its exact signed lock
  + a stale predecessor digest refuses the edit and requires a newly preserved source decision

& [ActivationUnitA] is validator dependency admission
  + predecessor is exact I02C completion and exact I03A Revision 1 signed activation
  + touches only workspace Cargo.toml Cargo.lock procedure-tool Cargo.toml and schema_validator_dependency.rs
  + proves exact jsonschema family lock no external resolver features no-resolution preflight denial and complete host debug and release gates
  + creates no production reader parser registry report or corpus behavior

& [ActivationUnitB] is faithful byte ingress
  + predecessor is completed A and separately signed I03B
  + adds json_ingress.rs and json_ingress.rs test then leases lib.rs for declaration and re-export only
  + performs no schema validation typed deserialization semantic function execution or runtime I/O

& [ActivationUnitC] is semantic residual registry
  + predecessor is completed B and separately signed I03C
  + adds residual_registry.rs and residual_registry.rs test then leases lib.rs for declaration and re-export only
  + registry query is pure and cannot invoke named functions

& [ActivationUnitD] is dual-reader observation
  + predecessor is completed A B C and separately signed I03D
  + adds reader_observation.rs and reader_observation.rs test then leases lib.rs for declaration and re-export only
  + owns CantorDenyRetriever and binds exact validator lock ingress registry and resource identities
  + forms observations and never compatibility admission

& [ActivationUnitE1] is obligation compilation
  + predecessor is completed D and separately signed I03E1
  + creates conformance/mod.rs if absent and adds obligation.rs and conformance_obligation.rs test
  + leases lib.rs and conformance/mod.rs only for declaration and re-export
  + compiler output is an obligation catalogue not a case expectation or result

& [ActivationUnitE2] is proposal generation
  + predecessor is completed E1 with exact obligation catalogue and separately signed I03E2
  + adds proposal.rs and conformance_proposal.rs test then leases conformance/mod.rs for declaration and re-export
  + generator output is unsigned proposal material and cannot authorize expectations

& [ActivationUnitE3] is oracle and review evidence
  + predecessor is completed E2 exact proposal catalogue future trust policy authorized principals and separately signed I03E3
  + adds review.rs and conformance_review.rs test then leases conformance/mod.rs for declaration and re-export
  + creates only verified review forms under trust policy and grants no reader execution

& [ActivationUnitE] is replay and report assembly
  + predecessor is completed D E1 E2 E3 and separately signed I03E
  + adds report.rs conformance_report.rs test and exact compile-time corpus inventory then leases conformance/mod.rs for declaration and re-export
  + execution is safe bounded effectless replay only and compatibility remains a separately admitted conclusion

& [DependencyDAG] is causal rather than merely numeric
  * I02C completion precedes A
  * A precedes B in activation queue and is a hard reader dependency of D
  * B precedes C in activation queue and B plus C are hard dependencies of D
  * D precedes E1
  * E1 precedes E2
  * E2 precedes E3
  * D E1 E2 and E3 precede E report assembly
  + no unit consumes documentary candidate output as if active

& [WorkerPartition] is lease based
  + one worker may own one activation unit and its exclusive module and test
  + an integration steward alone applies shared-ledger deltas after the owning unit produces an interface receipt
  + a fixture steward admits immutable catalogue entries after owner and review receipts
  + reviewers do not mutate the implementation they review
  + parallel work is allowed only when file sets and semantic prerequisites are disjoint

& [InterfaceReceipt] precedes integration
  + exact unit specification lock implementation commit module digest exported symbol set feature gate limits and error vocabulary
  + dependency imports and forbidden dependencies
  + test inventory and result identities
  + no integration lease is issued when the interface receipt is incomplete or challenged

& [ActivationEvidence] is unit local and aggregate
  + unit proof covers every requirement with implemented verified and satisfaction identities
  + shared-ledger proof reconstructs every lease predecessor delta and successor
  + dependency proof reconstructs the active predecessor chain
  + default and schema-conformance debug release format lint docs audit and evidence checks are recorded separately
  + host admission is execution evidence and never inferred from compilation alone

& [ChangeAndRecovery] preserve causality
  + a failed unit remains an immutable failed attempt with exact fault evidence
  + repair is a successor source diff review and proof rather than hidden overwrite
  + shared-ledger partial edits grant no downstream authority
  + rollback means selecting a reviewed predecessor state through a new commit not erasing history
  + any source path owner interface feature dependency fixture or execution-scope change requires renewed Source Preservation and SJS

& [ReadinessDisposition] is formation_ready_implementation_refused
  + module boundaries and activation queue may be specified now
  + I03A Enterprise signing release proof is absent
  + every I03 satisfaction signature and active implementation lock is absent
  + trust policy and reviewer catalogue required by E3 are absent
  + exact future corpus fixture inventory is absent
  + no source touch lease may issue from this source

& [NeverAuthority] is strict
  - never: Cargo mutation Rust implementation dependency activation untrusted parsing validation reader execution semantic invocation compatibility admission key generation signing provider model service persistence network notification effect production hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [RequestedProcessing] apply SJS semantic refinement constraint extraction data design seven-faculty review requirement support planning proof and inactive phase-lock formation to this exact source identity
